# Caddy auto-provisions and renews Let's Encrypt certs for any domain listed
# here — the only requirements are that APP_DOMAIN (set in infra/.env)
# actually resolves to this host's public IP, and ports 80/443 are open to
# the internet. The var must be non-empty — an unset `{$VAR}` is a hard parse
# error, unlike a normal shell default-expansion.
#
# Meilisearch and Ollama aren't listed here on purpose — see .env.example's
# comments on MEILISEARCH_HOST/OLLAMA_HOST. They're only ever called
# server-to-server (app -> meilisearch:7700, app -> ollama:11434 on the
# Docker network), so they never need a public hostname or TLS.

# App and MinIO's S3 API share one domain, split by path. MinIO MUST be
# publicly reachable: presigned download/preview URLs go straight to the end
# user's browser, not just server-to-server. Those URLs look like
# https://<APP_DOMAIN>/<MINIO_BUCKET>/<key>?X-Amz-..., which needs
# MINIO_ENDPOINT=https://<APP_DOMAIN> in the root .env. The path below MUST
# match MINIO_BUCKET (default fireflink-docs), and no app route may start
# with that name. reverse_proxy forwards the original Host header and path
# untouched, which is what keeps MinIO's signature check valid.
#
# Supabase Auth shares the domain too: the browser signs in by calling
# https://<APP_DOMAIN>/auth/v1/... directly (supabase-js builds its URLs from
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL), so with NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<APP_DOMAIN>
# those paths must reach Supabase's Kong gateway, not the app (which 404s
# them). Only /auth/v1/* is exposed; Studio, REST, realtime and the rest of
# Kong stay unreachable from outside. Needs this container on the
# supabase_default network (see docker-compose.yml) and no app route may
# start with /auth/v1.
{$APP_DOMAIN} {
	@storage path /fireflink-docs/*
	handle @storage {
		reverse_proxy minio:9000
	}

	@supabaseAuth path /auth/v1/*
	handle @supabaseAuth {
		reverse_proxy kong:8000
	}

	handle {
		reverse_proxy app:3000
	}
}

# MinIO's web console (bucket creation, browsing objects without SSHing in
# and using `mc`) — optional. Uncomment and add MINIO_CONSOLE_DOMAIN to
# infra/.env if you want it exposed; otherwise reach it via
# `docker compose exec minio mc ...` or an SSH tunnel to port 9001 instead.
#
# {$MINIO_CONSOLE_DOMAIN} {
# 	reverse_proxy minio:9001
# }
